sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P0 as Signed-in reader
    participant P1 as Web Application (Engagement UI)
    participant P2 as News controllers
    participant P3 as InteractionService
    participant P4 as Application Database
    P0->>P1: click Like
    P1->>P2: POST /news/{id}/like or /comments/{id}/like
    P2->>P2: authentication and throttle middleware
    P2->>P3: likeNews(userId, newsId) / likeComment(userId, commentId)
    P3->>P4: begin transaction, lock target, verify visibility
    P3->>P4: find existing like for this user and target
    P4-->>P3: return existing / absent
    alt [not liked]
    P3->>P4: insert likes / comment_likes row
    else [already liked]
    P3->>P4: delete existing like row
    end
    P3->>P4: count remaining likes
    P4-->>P3: return count
    opt [news post]
    P3->>P4: update news.likes_count
    end
    P3->>P4: commit
    P3-->>P2: return liked and likes_count
    P2-->>P1: JSON: liked, likes_count
    P1-->>P0: update Like state and count
    Note over P0,P4: Comment likes are counted directly, there is no cached comments.likes_count column. Unauthenticated requests stop at middleware. Short-video equivalents use ShortEngagementController and short_video_likes / short_video_comment_likes, with the same toggle pattern.
